BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Lost Founder: James Wilson and the Forgotten Fight for a Peopl
 e’s Constitution
DTSTART:20260805T220000Z
DTEND:20260806T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260801T065413Z
UID:79dccb63-d80b-5f05-b257-ef05b3179ca3
DESCRIPTION:Founding Father James Wilson’s bold vision for American demo
 cracy was lost to scandal. As a young lawyer\, Wilson made the case for Am
 erican independence in an essay that inspired the famous words “We hold 
 these truths to be self-evident\, that all men are created equal.” He wr
 ote the first draft of the Constitution and\, along with the much more fam
 ous James Madison\, played an essential role in its creation.\n\nMore info
  & tickets: https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2026-08-05/lost-founde
 r-james-wilson-and-forgotten-fight-peoples-constitution
LOCATION:Commonwealth Club World Affairs of California
URL:https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2026-08-05/lost-founder-james-
 wilson-and-forgotten-fight-peoples-constitution
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ecocivilization: Making a World That Works for All
DTSTART:20260806T003000Z
DTEND:20260806T023000Z
DTSTAMP:20260801T065413Z
UID:b790d89f-b5e8-59e0-b09c-f564ece67be3
DESCRIPTION:It has been said that it is easier to imagine the end of the w
 orld than it is to imagine the end of capitalism. Yet Jeremy Lent says tha
 t is what this historical moment urgently calls for. As climate chaos\, in
 equality and social fragmentation intensify\, humanity faces an imminent c
 hoice: continue with a system built on extraction and endless growth\, or 
 reimagine civilization itself. He says incremental policy improvements are
  no longer enough\, and what is needed is a deep transformation of our cur
 rent civilization to continue to survive.\n\nMore info & tickets: https://
 www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2026-08-05/ecocivilization-making-world-wo
 rks-all
LOCATION:The Commonwealth Club of California\, Toni Rembe Rock Auditorium\
 , San Francisco\, CA
URL:https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2026-08-05/ecocivilization-mak
 ing-world-works-all
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Investing in a Resilient Future: From Climate Finance to Human Hea
 lth
DTSTART:20260807T010000Z
DTEND:20260807T030000Z
DTSTAMP:20260801T065413Z
UID:d0807682-b9e6-518a-a7c2-c5708869e532
DESCRIPTION:Natural and human-made extreme weather events are disrupting f
 ood systems worldwide\, threatening the long-term economic stability and h
 ealth of already vulnerable populations. Across the globe\, 80 percent of 
 the poorest live in rural communities and rely on smallholder farming for 
 their household food and income. And smallholder farmers produce around on
 e-third of the total share of the world’s food\, yet are disproportionat
 ely affected by climate risks\, uncertainty\, and poverty\, often having l
 imited resources to adapt to these changes.\n\nMore info & tickets: https:
 //www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2026-08-06/investing-resilient-future-cl
 imate-finance-human-health
LOCATION:Commonwealth Club World Affairs of California\, 110 The Embarcade
 ro\, San Francisco\, CA
URL:https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2026-08-06/investing-resilient
 -future-climate-finance-human-health
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Author Event: When the Declaration of Independence Was News\, by E
 mily Sneff
DTSTART:20260807T013000Z
DTEND:20260807T033000Z
DTSTAMP:20260801T065413Z
UID:ed3532a0-8811-52aa-98a9-3163bb5068a7
DESCRIPTION:Join historian Emily Sneff for a presentation on the story beh
 ind the Declaration of Independence and how its message was shared in 1776
 .\nDrawing on her latest research\, Dr Sneff will explore how news of inde
 pendence spread across the colonies and beyond\, offering fresh insights i
 nto this pivotal moment in American history. This in-person event provides
  a wonderful opportunity to hear from the author and deepen your understan
 ding of the nation’s founding.\n\nMore info & tickets: https://www.commo
 nwealthclub.org/events/2026-08-06/author-event-when-declaration-independen
 ce-was-news-emily-sneff
LOCATION:Lafayette Public Library\, Don Tatzin Auditorium\, Lafayette\, CA
URL:https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2026-08-06/author-event-when-d
 eclaration-independence-was-news-emily-sneff
