BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Imperfect Circles Discussion Group at the Orinda Library
DTSTART:20260807T013000Z
DTEND:20260807T033000Z
DTSTAMP:20260801T065413Z
UID:51b2765d-d50a-5b44-8295-18eb4e93cb37
DESCRIPTION:Are you a person who never tires of talking or thinking about 
 philosophical\, scientific or religious theories? Are you interested in ps
 ychological insights\, or attempts at such insights\, into human life? The
 re are many who would insist that being realistic about human life means y
 ou should ignore such fundamental questions—starting around the time the
  ink dries on your diploma. But it is unrealistic to ignore the fundamenta
 l explanatory concepts that underlie each successful human civilization—
 concepts that sometimes help and sometimes hinder us in our pursuit of hap
 piness.\n\nMore info & tickets: https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/20
 26-08-06/imperfect-circles-discussion-group-orinda-library
LOCATION:Orinda Public Library\, 26 Orinda Way\, Orinda\, CA
URL:https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2026-08-06/imperfect-circles-d
 iscussion-group-orinda-library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sen. Adam Schiff: The “Cost of Corruption” Under Donald Trump\
 , and How Americans Are Paying the Price
DTSTART:20260810T200000Z
DTEND:20260810T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20260801T065413Z
UID:79a9f56d-fa7f-59a0-96c7-eb68ab312b02
DESCRIPTION:In a recent floor speech\, California Senator Adam Schiff outl
 ined ways he says that President Trump has used the presidency to enrich h
 imself and his family\, and how it’s driving up costs from gas to grocer
 ies for families. Schiff’s remarks came after the president reported mak
 ing more than $2 billion dollars in his first year in office\, mostly from
  cryptocurrency businesses. \n“The payments to the president and his fa
 mily have been massive\,” Schiff said. “The self-dealing and profiteer
 ing have been absolutely breathtaking in their scope.”\n\nMore info & ti
 ckets: https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2026-08-10/sen-adam-schiff-
 cost-corruption-under-donald-trump-and-how-americans-are-paying
LOCATION:Commonwealth Club World Affairs of California\, 110 The Embarcade
 ro\, San Francisco\, CA
URL:https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2026-08-10/sen-adam-schiff-cos
 t-corruption-under-donald-trump-and-how-americans-are-paying
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Race for Governor 2026\, The Final Stretch: Steve Hilton
DTSTART:20260811T010000Z
DTEND:20260811T030000Z
DTSTAMP:20260801T065413Z
UID:eabf949c-4458-59a1-abb9-247593ec8e53
DESCRIPTION:There were 61 candidates on California’s June primary ballot
  for governor\, but the race is now down to two: Republican Steve Hilton a
 nd Democrat Xavier Becerra. \nHilton is a former Fox News commentator and
  political advisor. He was endorsed by President Trump and promises to “
 restore the California Dream” by cutting government spending\, reducing 
 taxes and energy prices\, and slashing regulations. \nJoin us as Hilton d
 elivers a speech outlining his vision for the state and sits down for a co
 nversation with KQED’s Scott Shafer.\n\nMore info & tickets: https://www
 .commonwealthclub.org/events/2026-08-10/race-governor-2026-final-stretch-s
 teve-hilton
LOCATION:Commonwealth Club World Affairs of California\, 110 The Embarcade
 ro\, San Francisco\, CA
URL:https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2026-08-10/race-governor-2026-
 final-stretch-steve-hilton
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Balancing Public Safety & Civil Liberties in the Age of Innovation
DTSTART:20260812T190000Z
DTEND:20260812T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260801T065413Z
UID:3000a698-b478-5361-8c73-8ca9de47e74c
DESCRIPTION:Since the passage of Proposition E in 2024\, San Francisco has
  expanded its use of technology in public safety\, including drones\, auto
 mated license plate readers\, and the city’s new Real Time Investigation
 s Center. As these tools become part of everyday policing\, they’ve prom
 pted conversations about how the city can pursue safer streets while prote
 cting privacy and civil liberties.\n\nMore info & tickets: https://www.com
 monwealthclub.org/events/2026-08-12/balancing-public-safety-civil-libertie
 s-age-innovation
LOCATION:The Commonwealth Club of California\, Taube Family Auditorium\, S
 an Francisco\, CA
URL:https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2026-08-12/balancing-public-sa
 fety-civil-liberties-age-innovation
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ninety-Two: The Silent Revolt No One Saw Coming
DTSTART:20260814T010000Z
DTEND:20260814T030000Z
DTSTAMP:20260801T065413Z
UID:497aed42-ea02-5674-8013-31c3f0361a45
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an evening of film\, data and dialogue exploring o
 ne of the most consequential workforce questions of our time\, featuring t
 he documentary Ninety-Two: The Silent Revolt No One Saw Coming.\nBlack wom
 en are among the fastest-growing groups of breadwinners in America. Yet de
 spite their outsized contribution to families\, communities and the econom
 y\, they continue to experience disproportionate levels of burnout\, workp
 lace inequity\, financial strain and invisible labor.\nWhat happens when t
 he very people holding up the economy can no longer sustain the weight?\n\
 nMore info & tickets: https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2026-08-13/n
 inety-two-silent-revolt-no-one-saw-coming
LOCATION:The Commonwealth Club of California\, Taube Family Auditorium\, S
 an Francisco\, CA
URL:https://www.commonwealthclub.org/events/2026-08-13/ninety-two-silent-r
 evolt-no-one-saw-coming
END:VEVENT
